### Critical Risks

1.  **Data Corruption & Race Conditions**: The design is fundamentally unsafe. Multiple misses selecting the same slot concurrently will cause concurrent writes to the same buffer, corrupting data. Furthermore, returning a view into a shared buffer while another thread might be resizing or overwriting it creates severe data races. "Immutable objects" do not protect against concurrent mutation of the *cache storage*.
2.  **Unbounded Memory & OOM**: Resizing buffers based on unvalidated file headers allows malicious or corrupted files to trigger massive allocations, causing Out-Of-Memory crashes. There is no protection against integer overflows